OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCReflections on BBC One's COW
OL,4,Cera on its 40th anniversary
OL,5,
OL,6,FWhile relatively few programmes were
OL,7,Fsubtitled in 1985, the proportion
OL,8,Fquickly grew.
OL,10,FThen there is the question of the clock
OL,11,Fdesign?
OL,13,FWhy did Cardiff and Glasgow have a
OL,14,Fclock with a blue centre dot, matching
OL,15,Fthe design of the previous network
OL,16,Fclock and the BBC Two clock?
OL,18,FNetwork's clock had the dot missing.
OL,19,FThis was also the case in Northern
OL,20,FIreland.
OL,23,APub: 16-Feb-2025Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,130,120,200,300,0,100
PN,12906
SC,0006
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F129A1772999459
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G6/8
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCReflections on BBC One's COW
OL,4,Cera on its 40th anniversary
OL,5,
OL,6,FIt may not be coincidental that
OL,7,FNorthern Ireland's clock equipment was
OL,8,Fin use from the previous autumn and got
OL,9,Fupdated once the new look was
OL,10,Fintroduced.
OL,12,FWere Cardiff and Glasgow using an early
OL,13,Fdesign? And if so why was it not
OL,14,Fupdated?
OL,16,FOr was the "error" with network and
OL,17,FNorthern Ireland?
OL,19,FLook closely at the BBC One Wales COW
OL,20,Ftoo.
OL,23,APub: 16-Feb-2025Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,130,120,200,300,0,100
PN,12907
SC,0007
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F129A1772999459
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G7/8
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCReflections on BBC One's COW
OL,4,Cera on its 40th anniversary
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe shading of the '1' is slightly
OL,7,Fdifferent to other versions?
OL,9,FWas this deliberate design? Or an
OL,10,Ferror?
OL,12,FGiven that the channel in Wales was
OL,13,Fstill known as BBC Wales ` not BBC One
OL,14,FWales ` was consideration given to
OL,15,Famending the design? The name did not
OL,16,Fchange orally until around 1988.
OL,18,FScotland had been using the name BBC
OL,19,FScotland since October 1983 but changed
OL,20,Fthe name back to BBC One Scotland when
OL,21,Fthe COW debuted.
OL,23,APub: 16-Feb-2025Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,130,120,200,300,0,100
PN,12908
SC,0008
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F129A1772999459
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G8/8
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCReflections on BBC One's COW
OL,4,Cera on its 40th anniversary
OL,5,
OL,6,FFinally the way in which the nations
OL,7,Fmodified programme slides was
OL,8,Finconsistent. Did each nation just find
OL,9,Fits own way to amend the basic design?
OL,11,FIt's all fascinating.
OL,13,FThe COW ident was a revelation. In many
OL,14,Frespects, it represents timeless
OL,15,Felegance. A simple design which was
OL,16,Fbeautifully executed using what was
OL,17,Fthen cutting edge equipment.
OL,23,APub: 16-Feb-2025Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,130,120,200,300,0,100@
